NAME
    pager - select less when available, otherwise more

SYNOPSIS
    pager [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    pager is a thin terminal-pager wrapper.

    It selects less when less is available through the current command
    environment. Otherwise it selects more.

    With no file operands, the selected backend reads standard input.

    With one or more file operands, pager passes the operands unchanged and in
    their original order to the selected backend.

    pager does not inspect terminal state, resolve or validate file paths,
    pre-read or concatenate input, rewrite backend diagnostics, or normalize
    backend exit statuses. Interactive and redirected behavior therefore follow
    the selected backend.

BACKEND POLICY
    less
        Preferred whenever available.

    more
        Fallback when less is unavailable.

    Selection is based on command availability, not operating-system identity.

CALLER ENVIRONMENT
    pager preserves the caller environment.

    Variables consumed by the selected backend, including LESS, LESSOPEN and
    LESSCLOSE, are not cleared or rewritten.

    pager does not expose separate backend configuration or arbitrary backend
    command strings.

OPERANDS
    file
        File operand passed unchanged to the selected backend. Zero or more file
        operands are accepted.

EXIT STATUS
    The exit status is the status of the selected backend, or the shell
    execution-failure status if that backend cannot be executed. pager does not
    define a normalized backend-independent status mapping.

SEE ALSO
